{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L197","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:197"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Durable store for run lifecycle records."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"REQUIRED: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createOrResume"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"update"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"get"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"findActiveRun"},{"type":"text","value":". Every backend\nmust implement all four — they are what the persistence middleware calls\nunconditionally. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"findActiveRun"},{"type":"text","value":" is required rather than feature-detected\nbecause a backend that has not implemented it is indistinguishable from one\nwhose answer is legitimately "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":", so reconnect would silently do nothing\ninstead of failing at build time. It was optional for exactly one release\ncycle and cost precisely that."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OPTIONAL: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listByThread"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listByParentRun"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listReclaimable"},{"type":"text","value":". Each serves\none higher-level feature (thread history, subagent card reload, reclaim\nreaping) and callers feature-detect them, degrading when a backend omits\nthem."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"properties","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Properties"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"createorresume","children":[{"type":"text","value":"createOrResume"}]},{"type":"code","value":"createOrResume: (input) => Promise<RunRecord>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L208","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:208"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create a run record, or return the existing one unchanged if "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runId"},{"type":"text","value":" is\nalready present."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"INVARIANT (idempotency): an existing record is returned "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"unchanged"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and\nthe passed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"startedAt"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parentRunId"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subagentRunId"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":" are ignored. This is what makes resuming a\nrun safe. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":" defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'running'"},{"type":"text","value":" on first creation. The three\nlink fields are copied only on the first insert."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"input","children":[{"type":"text","value":"input"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Pick"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"RunRecord.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RunRecord"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"threadId\""},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"runId\""},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"startedAt\""},{"type":"text","value":"> & "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"object"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"RunRecord.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RunRecord"}]},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"findactiverun","children":[{"type":"text","value":"findActiveRun"}]},{"type":"code","value":"findActiveRun: (threadId) => Promise<RunRecord | null>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L287","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:287"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The most recent "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'running'"},{"type":"text","value":" run for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" if none is active."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"REQUIRED. This resolves \"does this thread have a live run to attach to?\"\nfrom the STABLE thread id, which is the durable basis for reconnecting a\nclient (a reload, or the same thread opened on another device) — independent\nof the ephemeral run id, which a single turn may mint several of. When more\nthan one run is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'running'"},{"type":"text","value":", the one with the greatest "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"startedAt"},{"type":"text","value":" wins."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A backend that stubs this to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" turns reconnect off silently, because\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" is also the correct answer for an idle thread. A backend with no run\nlifecycle at all should omit the whole "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runs"},{"type":"text","value":" store instead — capability\ntiers belong at the store level, not the method level."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"parameters-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"threadid","children":[{"type":"text","value":"threadId"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"RunRecord.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RunRecord"}]},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"get","children":[{"type":"text","value":"get"}]},{"type":"code","value":"get: (runId) => Promise<RunRecord | null>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L239","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:239"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Current record, or null when unknown."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"parameters-3","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"runid","children":[{"type":"text","value":"runId"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-3","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"RunRecord.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RunRecord"}]},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"listbyparentrun","children":[{"type":"text","value":"listByParentRun?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional listByParentRun?: (parentRunId) => Promise<RunRecord[]>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L253","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:253"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Child runs started by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parentRunId"},{"type":"text","value":", ascending by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"startedAt"},{"type":"text","value":".\nOPTIONAL. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reconstructChat"},{"type":"text","value":" uses this to put subagent cards back\non the parent assistant message. A store that omits it reloads the\ntext and not the cards."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"parameters-4","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"parentrunid","children":[{"type":"text","value":"parentRunId"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-4","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"RunRecord.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RunRecord"}]},{"type":"text","value":"[]>"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"listbythread","children":[{"type":"text","value":"listByThread?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional listByThread?: (threadId) => Promise<RunRecord[]>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L246","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:246"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every run in a conversation, ascending by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"startedAt"},{"type":"text","value":". OPTIONAL.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reconstructChat"},{"type":"text","value":" calls it to find the parent runs of children that a\ntool call started. Without it those cards stay absent on reload.\nConsumers feature-detect."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"parameters-5","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"threadid-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"threadId"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-5","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"RunRecord.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RunRecord"}]},{"type":"text","value":"[]>"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"listreclaimable","children":[{"type":"text","value":"listReclaimable?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional listReclaimable?: (opts) => Promise<RunRecord[]>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L269","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:269"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runs that may be reclaimed: ALL THREE of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status === 'running'"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"detachedSince"},{"type":"text","value":" is set, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"detachedSince <= now - ttlMs"},{"type":"text","value":". The cutoff is\n"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"inclusive"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — a run detached at exactly "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"now - ttlMs"},{"type":"text","value":" IS reclaimable."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OPTIONAL: only needed by a reaper. Consumers feature-detect."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"detachedSince"},{"type":"text","value":" is populated by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSandbox"},{"type":"text","value":"'s detach path (see\n"},{"type":"link","href":"RunRecord.md#detachedsince","children":[{"type":"text","value":"RunRecord.detachedSince"}]},{"type":"text","value":"). The sweep over the candidates this\nsurfaces is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-sandbox"},{"type":"text","value":"'s "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reapDetachedRuns"},{"type":"text","value":": it finalizes a run\nwhose agent already finished, expires one past its TTL, and reclaims the\nsandbox. That is a function, not a scheduler — the application invokes it\n(cron, queue, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"alarm()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"waitUntil"},{"type":"text","value":") — and a backend that omits this\nmethod cannot be reaped at all."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"parameters-6","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"opts","children":[{"type":"text","value":"opts"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":6,"id":"now","children":[{"type":"text","value":"now"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":6,"id":"ttlms","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ttlMs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-6","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"RunRecord.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RunRecord"}]},{"type":"text","value":"[]>"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"update","children":[{"type":"text","value":"update"}]},{"type":"code","value":"update: (runId, patch) => Promise<void>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L222","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:222"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Patch a record's mutable fields."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"INVARIANT: updating an unknown "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runId"},{"type":"text","value":" is a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"no-op"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — it must not throw\nand must not create a record."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"parameters-7","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"runid-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"runId"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"patch","children":[{"type":"text","value":"patch"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Partial"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Pick"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"RunRecord.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RunRecord"}]},{"type":"text","value":",\n| "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"status\""},{"type":"text","value":"\n| "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"finishedAt\""},{"type":"text","value":"\n| "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"error\""},{"type":"text","value":"\n| "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"usage\""},{"type":"text","value":"\n| "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"sandboxKey\""},{"type":"text","value":"\n| "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"detachedSince\""},{"type":"text","value":"\n| "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"cancelRequested\""},{"type":"text","value":"\n| "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"driverEpoch\""},{"type":"text","value":">>"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-7","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"properties","text":"Properties","level":2},{"id":"createorresume","text":"createOrResume","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"input","text":"input","level":5},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"findactiverun","text":"findActiveRun","level":3},{"id":"parameters-2","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"threadid","text":"threadId","level":5},{"id":"returns-2","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"get","text":"get","level":3},{"id":"parameters-3","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"runid","text":"runId","level":5},{"id":"returns-3","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"listbyparentrun","text":"listByParentRun?","level":3},{"id":"parameters-4","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"parentrunid","text":"parentRunId","level":5},{"id":"returns-4","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"listbythread","text":"listByThread?","level":3},{"id":"parameters-5","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"threadid-2","text":"threadId","level":5},{"id":"returns-5","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"listreclaimable","text":"listReclaimable?","level":3},{"id":"parameters-6","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"opts","text":"opts","level":5},{"id":"now","text":"now","level":6},{"id":"ttlms","text":"ttlMs","level":6},{"id":"returns-6","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"update","text":"update","level":3},{"id":"parameters-7","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"runid-2","text":"runId","level":5},{"id":"patch","text":"patch","level":5},{"id":"returns-7","text":"Returns","level":4}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:197](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L197)\n\nDurable store for run lifecycle records.\n\nREQUIRED: `createOrResume`, `update`, `get`, `findActiveRun`. Every backend\nmust implement all four — they are what the persistence middleware calls\nunconditionally. `findActiveRun` is required rather than feature-detected\nbecause a backend that has not implemented it is indistinguishable from one\nwhose answer is legitimately `null`, so reconnect would silently do nothing\ninstead of failing at build time. It was optional for exactly one release\ncycle and cost precisely that.\n\nOPTIONAL: `listByThread`, `listByParentRun`, `listReclaimable`. Each serves\none higher-level feature (thread history, subagent card reload, reclaim\nreaping) and callers feature-detect them, degrading when a backend omits\nthem.\n\n## Properties\n\n### createOrResume\n\n```ts\ncreateOrResume: (input) => Promise<RunRecord>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:208](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L208)\n\nCreate a run record, or return the existing one unchanged if `runId` is\nalready present.\n\nINVARIANT (idempotency): an existing record is returned **unchanged** and\nthe passed `threadId`, `startedAt`, `status`, `parentRunId`,\n`subagentRunId`, and `name` are ignored. This is what makes resuming a\nrun safe. `status` defaults to `'running'` on first creation. The three\nlink fields are copied only on the first insert.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### input\n\n`Pick`\\<[`RunRecord`](RunRecord.md), `\"threadId\"` \\| `\"runId\"` \\| `\"startedAt\"`\\> & `object`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<[`RunRecord`](RunRecord.md)\\>\n\n***\n\n### findActiveRun\n\n```ts\nfindActiveRun: (threadId) => Promise<RunRecord | null>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:287](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L287)\n\nThe most recent `'running'` run for `threadId`, or `null` if none is active.\n\nREQUIRED. This resolves \"does this thread have a live run to attach to?\"\nfrom the STABLE thread id, which is the durable basis for reconnecting a\nclient (a reload, or the same thread opened on another device) — independent\nof the ephemeral run id, which a single turn may mint several of. When more\nthan one run is `'running'`, the one with the greatest `startedAt` wins.\n\nA backend that stubs this to `null` turns reconnect off silently, because\n`null` is also the correct answer for an idle thread. A backend with no run\nlifecycle at all should omit the whole `runs` store instead — capability\ntiers belong at the store level, not the method level.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### threadId\n\n`string`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<[`RunRecord`](RunRecord.md) \\| `null`\\>\n\n***\n\n### get\n\n```ts\nget: (runId) => Promise<RunRecord | null>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:239](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L239)\n\nCurrent record, or null when unknown.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### runId\n\n`string`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<[`RunRecord`](RunRecord.md) \\| `null`\\>\n\n***\n\n### listByParentRun?\n\n```ts\noptional listByParentRun?: (parentRunId) => Promise<RunRecord[]>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:253](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L253)\n\nChild runs started by `parentRunId`, ascending by `startedAt`.\nOPTIONAL. `reconstructChat` uses this to put subagent cards back\non the parent assistant message. A store that omits it reloads the\ntext and not the cards.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### parentRunId\n\n`string`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<[`RunRecord`](RunRecord.md)[]\\>\n\n***\n\n### listByThread?\n\n```ts\noptional listByThread?: (threadId) => Promise<RunRecord[]>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:246](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L246)\n\nEvery run in a conversation, ascending by `startedAt`. OPTIONAL.\n`reconstructChat` calls it to find the parent runs of children that a\ntool call started. Without it those cards stay absent on reload.\nConsumers feature-detect.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### threadId\n\n`string`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<[`RunRecord`](RunRecord.md)[]\\>\n\n***\n\n### listReclaimable?\n\n```ts\noptional listReclaimable?: (opts) => Promise<RunRecord[]>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:269](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L269)\n\nRuns that may be reclaimed: ALL THREE of `status === 'running'`,\n`detachedSince` is set, and `detachedSince <= now - ttlMs`. The cutoff is\n**inclusive** — a run detached at exactly `now - ttlMs` IS reclaimable.\n\nOPTIONAL: only needed by a reaper. Consumers feature-detect.\n\n`detachedSince` is populated by `withSandbox`'s detach path (see\n[RunRecord.detachedSince](RunRecord.md#detachedsince)). The sweep over the candidates this\nsurfaces is `@tanstack/ai-sandbox`'s `reapDetachedRuns`: it finalizes a run\nwhose agent already finished, expires one past its TTL, and reclaims the\nsandbox. That is a function, not a scheduler — the application invokes it\n(cron, queue, `alarm()`, `waitUntil`) — and a backend that omits this\nmethod cannot be reaped at all.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### opts\n\n###### now\n\n`number`\n\n###### ttlMs\n\n`number`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<[`RunRecord`](RunRecord.md)[]\\>\n\n***\n\n### update\n\n```ts\nupdate: (runId, patch) => Promise<void>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:222](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L222)\n\nPatch a record's mutable fields.\n\nINVARIANT: updating an unknown `runId` is a **no-op** — it must not throw\nand must not create a record.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### runId\n\n`string`\n\n##### patch\n\n`Partial`\\<`Pick`\\<[`RunRecord`](RunRecord.md), \n  \\| `\"status\"`\n  \\| `\"finishedAt\"`\n  \\| `\"error\"`\n  \\| `\"usage\"`\n  \\| `\"sandboxKey\"`\n  \\| `\"detachedSince\"`\n  \\| `\"cancelRequested\"`\n  \\| `\"driverEpoch\"`\\>\\>\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<`void`\\>\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: RunStore\ntitle: RunStore\n---\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:197](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L197)\n\nDurable store for run lifecycle records.\n\nREQUIRED: `createOrResume`, `update`, `get`, `findActiveRun`. Every backend\nmust implement all four — they are what the persistence middleware calls\nunconditionally. `findActiveRun` is required rather than feature-detected\nbecause a backend that has not implemented it is indistinguishable from one\nwhose answer is legitimately `null`, so reconnect would silently do nothing\ninstead of failing at build time. It was optional for exactly one release\ncycle and cost precisely that.\n\nOPTIONAL: `listByThread`, `listByParentRun`, `listReclaimable`. Each serves\none higher-level feature (thread history, subagent card reload, reclaim\nreaping) and callers feature-detect them, degrading when a backend omits\nthem.\n\n## Properties\n\n### createOrResume\n\n```ts\ncreateOrResume: (input) => Promise<RunRecord>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:208](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L208)\n\nCreate a run record, or return the existing one unchanged if `runId` is\nalready present.\n\nINVARIANT (idempotency): an existing record is returned **unchanged** and\nthe passed `threadId`, `startedAt`, `status`, `parentRunId`,\n`subagentRunId`, and `name` are ignored. This is what makes resuming a\nrun safe. `status` defaults to `'running'` on first creation. The three\nlink fields are copied only on the first insert.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### input\n\n`Pick`\\<[`RunRecord`](RunRecord.md), `\"threadId\"` \\| `\"runId\"` \\| `\"startedAt\"`\\> & `object`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<[`RunRecord`](RunRecord.md)\\>\n\n***\n\n### findActiveRun\n\n```ts\nfindActiveRun: (threadId) => Promise<RunRecord | null>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:287](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L287)\n\nThe most recent `'running'` run for `threadId`, or `null` if none is active.\n\nREQUIRED. This resolves \"does this thread have a live run to attach to?\"\nfrom the STABLE thread id, which is the durable basis for reconnecting a\nclient (a reload, or the same thread opened on another device) — independent\nof the ephemeral run id, which a single turn may mint several of. When more\nthan one run is `'running'`, the one with the greatest `startedAt` wins.\n\nA backend that stubs this to `null` turns reconnect off silently, because\n`null` is also the correct answer for an idle thread. A backend with no run\nlifecycle at all should omit the whole `runs` store instead — capability\ntiers belong at the store level, not the method level.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### threadId\n\n`string`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<[`RunRecord`](RunRecord.md) \\| `null`\\>\n\n***\n\n### get\n\n```ts\nget: (runId) => Promise<RunRecord | null>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:239](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L239)\n\nCurrent record, or null when unknown.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### runId\n\n`string`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<[`RunRecord`](RunRecord.md) \\| `null`\\>\n\n***\n\n### listByParentRun?\n\n```ts\noptional listByParentRun?: (parentRunId) => Promise<RunRecord[]>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:253](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L253)\n\nChild runs started by `parentRunId`, ascending by `startedAt`.\nOPTIONAL. `reconstructChat` uses this to put subagent cards back\non the parent assistant message. A store that omits it reloads the\ntext and not the cards.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### parentRunId\n\n`string`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<[`RunRecord`](RunRecord.md)[]\\>\n\n***\n\n### listByThread?\n\n```ts\noptional listByThread?: (threadId) => Promise<RunRecord[]>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:246](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L246)\n\nEvery run in a conversation, ascending by `startedAt`. OPTIONAL.\n`reconstructChat` calls it to find the parent runs of children that a\ntool call started. Without it those cards stay absent on reload.\nConsumers feature-detect.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### threadId\n\n`string`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<[`RunRecord`](RunRecord.md)[]\\>\n\n***\n\n### listReclaimable?\n\n```ts\noptional listReclaimable?: (opts) => Promise<RunRecord[]>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:269](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L269)\n\nRuns that may be reclaimed: ALL THREE of `status === 'running'`,\n`detachedSince` is set, and `detachedSince <= now - ttlMs`. The cutoff is\n**inclusive** — a run detached at exactly `now - ttlMs` IS reclaimable.\n\nOPTIONAL: only needed by a reaper. Consumers feature-detect.\n\n`detachedSince` is populated by `withSandbox`'s detach path (see\n[RunRecord.detachedSince](RunRecord.md#detachedsince)). The sweep over the candidates this\nsurfaces is `@tanstack/ai-sandbox`'s `reapDetachedRuns`: it finalizes a run\nwhose agent already finished, expires one past its TTL, and reclaims the\nsandbox. That is a function, not a scheduler — the application invokes it\n(cron, queue, `alarm()`, `waitUntil`) — and a backend that omits this\nmethod cannot be reaped at all.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### opts\n\n###### now\n\n`number`\n\n###### ttlMs\n\n`number`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<[`RunRecord`](RunRecord.md)[]\\>\n\n***\n\n### update\n\n```ts\nupdate: (runId, patch) => Promise<void>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:222](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L222)\n\nPatch a record's mutable fields.\n\nINVARIANT: updating an unknown `runId` is a **no-op** — it must not throw\nand must not create a record.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### runId\n\n`string`\n\n##### patch\n\n`Partial`\\<`Pick`\\<[`RunRecord`](RunRecord.md), \n  \\| `\"status\"`\n  \\| `\"finishedAt\"`\n  \\| `\"error\"`\n  \\| `\"usage\"`\n  \\| `\"sandboxKey\"`\n  \\| `\"detachedSince\"`\n  \\| `\"cancelRequested\"`\n  \\| `\"driverEpoch\"`\\>\\>\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<`void`\\>\n"}
